{
  "requirement": "Habeas MUST resolve its saved configuration before constructing Rig provider\nclients and completion models. The Habeas data structures MUST remain the saved\nformat. Rig model references MAY be reused internally without discarding the\nconnection settings they do not represent.\n\nThe Bedrock adapter MUST pass the chosen AWS profile and region through AWS SDK\nconfiguration. The Ollama adapter MUST use the chosen server, exact model ID,\nand optional authentication; the server MAY be local or remote. Both adapters\nMUST supply the same tools and initial prompt.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "Saved Habeas configuration remains distinct from runtime provider clients. RigProvider maps the selected profile/region through the AWS SDK and maps exact Ollama model, endpoint, and optional bearer credential to Rig native completion. Local Bedrock signing and Ollama request assertions verify the concrete adapter mapping, standard and backend-specific inference settings, and common tools/prompt.",
  "inputs": [
